// STEP 1 - MEASURE the actual current behavior, without assuming
db.products.find({ category: 'electronics', inStock: true }).explain('executionStats');
// Output shows: totalDocsExamined: 50000, nReturned: 230,
// executionTimeMillis: 145
// DIAGNOSIS: examining 50,000 documents to return only 230 matches
// is a strong, concrete signal of a missing, genuinely useful index -
// not assumption, actual measured evidence

// STEP 2 - CREATE a compound index matching the actual query's
// combined filter conditions (both fields used together)
db.products.createIndex({ category: 1, inStock: 1 });

// STEP 3 - RE-MEASURE to confirm the index genuinely helped
db.products.find({ category: 'electronics', inStock: true }).explain('executionStats');
// Output now shows: totalDocsExamined: 230, nReturned: 230,
// executionTimeMillis: 3
// CONFIRMED: totalDocsExamined now matches nReturned almost exactly,
// and executionTimeMillis dropped from 145ms to 3ms - the index
// genuinely, measurably solved the diagnosed problem

